                 "This is the step most beginners get stuck on, and it is rarely about technique. People stop because they do not know how a tee time works, what to wear, how fast to play or what happens if they hit it sideways in front of strangers. Every one of those worries is normal and every one of them is answerable in about five minutes.",
                 "We take beginners out onto the course at Ormonde Fields once you can make contact reliably, often playing three or four holes rather than eighteen. You learn <strong>course management</strong>, pace of play, where to stand, how to keep score and the handful of etiquette rules that actually matter, all in the place they apply rather than in a bay.",
