            {"type": "prose", "kick": "Honest answers",
             "h2": "How Long Does It Take to <em>Learn Golf?</em>",
             "blocks": [
                 ("h3", "How Long Before I Can Hit the Ball Consistently?"),
                 ("p", "Most beginners are getting a wedge airborne inside their first session and hitting a seven iron with some regularity within three or four. Consistency across a full set takes longer, generally three to six months of occasional practice. Anyone quoting you a fortnight is selling something. The pace depends far more on how often you practise than on natural talent, which is genuinely good news for most of us."),
                 ("h3", "How Long Until I Can Play a Full Round?"),
                 ("p", "Six to twelve lessons and a bit of practice will usually get you round nine holes without feeling out of place. A full eighteen is more about stamina and pace of play than technique. Playing a few holes with a coach first, as part of on-course work, shortens that timeline considerably because the worry rather than the swing is what holds people back."),
                 ("h3", "What Golf Etiquette Do I Actually Need to Know?"),
                 ("p", "Less than you fear. Keep up with the group in front rather than worrying about the group behind. Stand still and stay quiet while somebody is swinging, and stay out of their eyeline. Repair your pitch mark on the green and rake the bunker after you. Shout if a ball is heading anywhere near another person. That short list covers ninety per cent of it, and nobody at a golf club minds a beginner who is trying."),
                 ("h3", "Am I Too Old to Start Playing Golf?"),
                 ("p", "No, and this comes up constantly. Golf is one of the few sports where people take it up in their fifties and sixties and still improve for years. If mobility is a concern, a <a href=\"tpi-screening.html\">TPI screening</a> shows what your body can currently do, and the swing is then built to suit you rather than to suit a tour player. Work in the <a href=\"golf-fitness.html\">golf fitness suite</a> can widen those limits over time."),
                 ("p", "Beginners come to the academy from Derby, Nottingham, Ripley, Heanor, Alfreton and across Derbyshire and Nottinghamshire, and a fair number arrive having been given a set of clubs they have never used. That is a perfectly reasonable way to begin. If you would rather see the whole picture first, the <a href=\"faqs.html\">FAQs page</a> answers most of the practical questions people ask before booking."),
             ], "alt": True},

