            {"type": "faq", "kick": "Common questions",
             "h2": "Beginner Golf Lessons Derby &amp; Nottingham - <em>FAQs.</em>",
             "qs": [
                 ("Do I need my own golf clubs for a beginner lesson?",
                  "No. Clubs are provided for beginner sessions at no extra cost, so you can arrive with nothing and still have a full lesson. We would actively rather you did not buy a set before someone has watched you swing, because the wrong shaft or the wrong lie angle builds faults that then need coaching out later."),
                 ("How much does a beginner golf lesson cost near Derby?",
                  "A one to one beginner lesson is £55 for sixty minutes with an Advanced PGA Professional, clubs included. If you plan to keep going, the <a href=\"monthly-programme.html\">monthly coaching programme</a> is £60 a month and suits beginners better, because frequent small steps beat one lesson followed by three months of guessing."),
                 ("I have literally never played. Is that a problem?",
                  "It is the most common starting point we see. Beginner coaching assumes zero knowledge, zero equipment and zero fitness. The first session covers grip, stance and a half swing with a wedge, and the goal is simply that you strike some golf balls and enjoy the hour enough to book another."),
                 ("Will people be watching me?",
                  "Beginner lessons run in a private indoor <a href=\"trackman-teaching-bay.html\">teaching bay</a> with the door shut, so no. This is the single most common worry new golfers raise and it is worth answering directly. When you are ready to hit outside, the covered range bays are separated from one another as well."),
                 ("What should I wear to my first golf lesson?",
                  "Comfortable clothing you can rotate in and trainers with reasonable grip. No golf shoes required and no dress code to trip over. If you plan to go out onto the course later, a collared shirt is the usual expectation at most clubs, but that has nothing to do with your first lesson in a bay."),
                 ("How many lessons will I need before I can play a round?",
                  "Six to twelve is the honest range for nine holes, depending how often you practise in between. Practice matters more than lesson count. Two twenty minute sessions on the <a href=\"trackman-range.html\">driving range</a> each week will get you there far quicker than a lesson a fortnight and nothing else."),
                 ("Would a group be better than a one to one lesson?",
                  "It depends on you. Groups are cheaper, more sociable and less intense, which is why <a href=\"get-into-golf.html\">Get Into Golf</a> exists. One to one is faster, because the whole hour is spent on your swing rather than shared out. Plenty of beginners start in a group and move to individual coaching once they are hooked."),
                 ("Am I too old or too unfit to learn golf?",
                  "Almost certainly not. Golf accommodates a wide range of physical ability, and the swing can be built around what your body will actually do. A <a href=\"tpi-screening.html\">TPI movement screening</a> establishes that starting point precisely, rather than assuming you should be able to make a tour-length backswing."),
                 ("Where are you and how do I get there from Nottingham?",
                  "Evolution Golf Academy is at Ormonde Fields Golf Club, Nottingham Road, Codnor, Ripley DE5 9RJ, about twenty minutes from Nottingham and fifteen from Derby along the A610. Parking is free. Full directions are on the <a href=\"location.html\">location page</a>."),
             ], "alt": True}
