            {"type": "prose", "kick": "Structured coaching, not one-offs",
             "h2": "What Is a <em>Monthly Golf Coaching Programme?</em>",
             "blocks": [
                 ("p", "The <strong>monthly golf coaching programme</strong> replaces the stop-start pattern most golfers fall into. Instead of buying a lesson when something goes badly wrong, panicking about it for an hour and then disappearing for four months, you have continuous contact with the same PGA Professional, a plan that runs across a season and a record of your numbers that goes back further than your memory does."),
                 ("p", "It costs £60 a month. That is deliberately close to the price of a single one to one session, because the point of the programme is regularity rather than volume. Golfers who see a coach every few weeks improve at a completely different rate to golfers who see one twice a year, and the difference has very little to do with how much talent either has."),
                 ("h3", "How Is It Different From Booking Individual Lessons?"),
                 ("p", "A one-off lesson has to solve something inside sixty minutes, which pushes both coach and golfer towards quick fixes. A programme does not carry that pressure. Your coach can spend a session establishing what your body will allow, another rebuilding the strike, and a third moving that change onto the course, knowing you will be back. Bigger, more durable changes become possible because nobody is trying to make them stick in one hour."),
                 ("p", "The second difference is memory. On a programme your coach knows what you were working on in February, what your carry numbers looked like then, and which drill you never got round to doing. That continuity is worth more than most golfers expect, and it is the main reason people who move from single <a href=\"1-1-lessons.html\">1:1 golf lessons</a> onto the programme rarely go back."),
                 ("h3", "What Is Included Each Month?"),
                 ("p", "Regular coaching sessions with your PGA Professional, a written practice plan between each one, Trackman data captured and stored session by session, and video kept so you can compare where you are now to where you started. Your coach also builds your practice around what you can genuinely fit in, whether that is three sessions a week on the <a href=\"trackman-range.html\">Trackman driving range</a> or twenty minutes on a Sunday."),
                 ("p", "Where a physical restriction is holding back a change, a <a href=\"tpi-screening.html\">TPI movement screening</a> and follow-on work in the <a href=\"golf-fitness.html\">golf fitness suite</a> get folded into the same plan, so the coaching and the conditioning point in the same direction instead of fighting one another."),
             ]},

