            {"type": "prose", "kick": "Who benefits",
             "h2": "Who Should Have a <em>TPI Screening?</em>",
             "blocks": [
                 ("h3", "Golfers Who Keep Making the Same Fault"),
                 ("p", "If a fault returns within two weeks of every lesson, technique is probably not the problem. Early extension and loss of posture in particular are usually the body finding a way round a restriction. Screening tells you which restriction, and at that point the fault stops being a mystery and starts being a solvable one. This is the largest single group who benefit."),
                 ("h3", "Golfers With Back, Hip or Shoulder Trouble"),
                 ("p", "The golf swing asks a lot of the lower back, and a body that cannot rotate through the hips and thoracic spine will take that rotation from the lumbar spine instead, which it is not designed to provide. A screen identifies that pattern before it becomes an injury. Screening is an assessment rather than medical treatment, and anything clinical gets referred on rather than guessed at."),
                 ("h3", "Golfers Chasing Distance"),
                 ("p", "Clubhead speed is produced by sequencing and by the range through which you can accelerate. If your hips will not rotate internally, or your lead shoulder will not reach across, you are capped regardless of effort. A screen shows where the ceiling is and the <a href=\"golf-fitness.html\">golf fitness suite</a> is where you go and raise it. Speed work on top of a restriction just produces a faster bad movement."),
                 ("h3", "Golfers Over Fifty, and Juniors"),
                 ("p", "Both ends of the range gain a lot. Older golfers get a swing built around what their body currently allows rather than one copied from a twenty-five year old tour player. Juniors get movement quality established early, which prevents years of compensation. Will Painter runs the <a href=\"junior-academy.html\">junior academy</a> and says when a screen would be worthwhile for a young player."),
                 ("p", "Golfers come for screening and fitting from Derby, Nottingham, Ripley, Belper, Heanor and across Derbyshire and Nottinghamshire. The academy is fifteen minutes from Derby and twenty from Nottingham on the A610, open 7am to 8pm daily, with free parking. Both screening and fitting need booking in advance, unlike the walk-in <a href=\"trackman-range.html\">Trackman range</a>."),
             ], "alt": True},

